---
Agent hooks: tell a session in a registered project how to run commands, and refuse writing a .env file there

Usage: kagebunshin hook [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  install        Set up the hooks for a coding agent
  session-start  Run by the agent when a session starts: tells it how this folder gets its secrets
  pre-tool-use   Run by the agent before a tool call: refuses writing a .env file in a registered project
  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json            Print machine-readable JSON; errors go to stderr as JSON
      --socket <PATH>   Daemon socket [default: $KAGEBUNSHIN_SOCKET, else a per-user runtime dir]
      --env <ENV>       Environment to use instead of the project's default
      --project <NAME>  Project to use instead of the one for this folder; it must claim this checkout's remotes
  -h, --help            Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version         Print version
